hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2876","**\nNarrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram, who said: 'Isa informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, who said: Muhammad—meaning Ibn Bakr—informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who informed us, on the authority of Abu'z-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (RA) say:\n\n\The Prophet (ﷺ) would stone the Jamarat on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm an-Nahr) during the forenoon (Dhuha).\""\n\nMa'mar also narrated one (stone)—meaning one Jamrah—and they both said:\n\n\""As for after that"," it is at the time when the sun declines (i.e."," after midday).\"""""
